Subject: Nightingale Update - Priority One

Agent Kepler,

Received your comm regarding the Bucharest anomaly. Situation is…complicated. The “collector,” as locals refer to him, isn’t dealing in antiquities as initially reported. It’s biological material. Specifically, highly modified avian DNA. Think accelerated evolution, weaponized migratory patterns. The samples aren’t just from local species either. We’ve identified genetic markers originating from the Amazon, Siberia, even isolated islands in the Pacific. He’s building something, and it’s not a museum exhibit.

My cover as a ornithological researcher is holding, barely. The collector, a man named Volkov, is meticulous. Surveillance is a nightmare – layers of security, rotating personnel, and a disturbing fondness for trained raptors. I’ve managed to infiltrate his outer perimeter, posing as a potential buyer of “rare specimens,” but getting close to the lab itself is proving impossible. 

The lab is located beneath a seemingly abandoned textile factory on the outskirts of the city. I’ve mapped the ventilation system – a potential entry point, but heavily guarded by pressure sensors and, predictably, more birds. I need a distraction, something significant enough to pull security away from the factory for at least thirty minutes. Your expertise in… unconventional tactics would be invaluable.

I’ve attached a schematic of the factory layout, including known sensor placements and guard patrol routes. Also included are preliminary analyses of the avian DNA samples I’ve managed to acquire – the modifications are… unsettling. They suggest a deliberate attempt to enhance flight endurance, navigational accuracy, and, most worryingly, aggression. 

The local authorities are oblivious, dismissing the increased bird activity as a seasonal migration pattern. We’re operating completely off the grid. Contacting HQ is too risky – Volkov has sophisticated jamming equipment. This channel is our only lifeline.

I suspect Volkov isn’t working alone. There are whispers of a shadowy organization known as “Aether,” rumored to be involved in bio-weaponry research. If this is true, the stakes are far higher than we initially anticipated. 

Requesting immediate authorization for Operation Skyfall – a coordinated disruption of the factory’s power grid. It’s a risky maneuver, but it’s our best chance of gaining access to the lab and securing the samples. 

Await your instructions. Time is of the essence. The birds are already changing.

Nightingale.



